{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">2021 AMC 10A #16</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2021 AMC 12A #16</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the following list of numbers, the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> times in the list for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917e3430450e9049864739d088103bef0598a899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq n \\leq 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4f50e6ad3c33b14e7352b50ecc5ff8322c37702.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4, \\ldots, 200, 200, \\ldots , 200\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"16\" />What is the median of the numbers in this list?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27afcb54267a25ea77122e679919832098e78f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~100.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~134 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~142 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~150.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~167$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"468\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92728df69bac90147fdb422ef18ed57f40fb787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+..+199+200=\\frac{(200)(201)}{2}=20100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"351\" height=\"38\" /> numbers in total. Let the median be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. We want to find the median <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8ccc066133aa10fee023edbde69d3985904d2dde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k(k+1)}{2}=20100/2,\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad0ae4f03a0fffc0b86e7b36b3ce0895d9e703b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k(k+1)=20100.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428305397f26b037becffbf34a767b119a04f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{20100} \\approx 142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging this value in as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5bbc3647259e660c3606f8ce0cedfa76a9cff51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(142)(143)=10153.\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e009a1faf20c9d17dad000f3b5f3b44d9f3a9514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10153-142&lt;10050$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"163\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e457abc5e55d562a8e426b0d19d8d006c9c06ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$152$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />nd and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f152e2688863b88e971932e82c28adec9063a05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$153$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />rd numbers, and hence, our desired answer. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afefb3569f51abfaeb25370231a2f9a8f724045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(C) 142}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"67\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Note that we can derive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428305397f26b037becffbf34a767b119a04f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{20100} \\approx 142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> through the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38c04f868404d0ae2801c0b7dc4c55e84d07898.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{n} = \\sqrt{a+b} \\approx \\sqrt{a} + \\frac{b}{2\\sqrt{a} + 1},\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"42\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a perfect square less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6fda9ee736a83793e8fdd874a2885921de7645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19600$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e4790acf8c0c7f8a0bb1e84ab5a4e93bdaa17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a} = 140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121467f0ecf89e046dd205bef38b128062efdcf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 500$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />. We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a841024197d6d0d17b605431dea63ff649f7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\approx 140 + \\frac{500}{2(140)+1} \\approx 142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"221\" height=\"42\" />. ~approximation by ciceronii\n</p><p>Note by Fasolinka (use answer choices): Once you know that the answer is in the 140s range (200,000 is around 14^2 times 10^2) by the approximation, it is highly improbable for the answer to be anything but C.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />th number of this sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6389c3d7d4f1bf48afee580c29ff4b8f21026b5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lceil\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{1+8x}}{2}\\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"131\" height=\"44\" /> via the quadratic formula. We can see that if we halve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> we end up getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d532be28170fb4e06e6cee5a3171934a3a11ad50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lceil\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{1+4x}}{2}\\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"131\" height=\"44\" />. This is approximately the number divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/512c13326765c5cde6b97a9a886cfb0174326c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{200}{\\sqrt{2}} = 141.4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"96\" height=\"42\" /> and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> looks like the only number close to it, it is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/b/48bc12311c0d19a7c68bfb66f483cdf09754e5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C) 142}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"67\" height=\"29\" /> ~Lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can look at answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> first. That means that the number of numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is roughly the number of numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f61021f12ab09c5b9c3cfbcd7f6207920ff765b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$143$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The number of numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8614c1b3993e78519131182767d0a43ea0714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27809f6b8ee4d02c21fdf73207113c0ff62980c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{142(142+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" /> which is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197284a4db127c2aab1fda1f7792e55bd687bad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> The number of numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f61021f12ab09c5b9c3cfbcd7f6207920ff765b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$143$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e98a1a6eb60a3f81d9efd4272361ad8b7a3ec6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{200(200+1)}{2}-\\frac{142(142+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"228\" height=\"38\" /> which is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f4f407fa86791b87ad5286ea377c10b2111d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> as well. Therefore, we can be relatively sure the answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c9930632ed8282fdb94b5417fc2249cc82a5351b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~142}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:PureSwag\" title=\"User:PureSwag\">PureSwag</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Geometry)\">Solution 4 (Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can arrange the numbers in the following pattern:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6cd89ce0923135d72793b5bff6097f760155e04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\begin{array}{cccccc} \\ &amp;\\ &amp;\\ &amp;\\ &amp;\\ 200 &amp; \\\\ \\ &amp;\\ &amp;\\ &amp;\\ 199 &amp; \\ 200 &amp; \\\\ \\ &amp;\\ &amp;\\ \\iddots&amp; \\ \\vdots&amp; \\ \\vdots&amp; \\\\ \\ &amp;\\ 2&amp; \\ \\cdots&amp; \\ 199&amp; \\ 200&amp; \\\\ 1 &amp; \\ 2 &amp; \\ \\cdots&amp; \\ 199&amp; \\ 200&amp; \\end{array} \\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"105\" />\n</p><p>We can see this as a isosceles right triangle, with legs of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/6/2e6a0c2f300ca8335e5b945617a0faed2a1ad5cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d73f9f7d38f90c0d25d4776ef1774e28a6851d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,0)--(200,200)--(200,0)--cycle); draw((142,0)--(142,142)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(142,0)--(142,142),E); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(0,0)--(142,0),S); label(&quot;$200$&quot;,(200,0)--(200,200),E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length such that both sides of the triangle have the same area. The desired answer is then around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> because about half of the numbers in the list fall on each side.\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/e/9de06c0aadfe80934f4426119f3abde22cd293f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{x^2}{2} =&amp; \\:\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{200^2}{2} \\\\ x^2 =&amp; \\:\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 200^2 \\\\ x =&amp; \\:\\frac{200}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\: 100\\sqrt{2} \\approx 141. \\end{align*}\" width=\"209\" height=\"129\" />\nWe see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/8/3e839dced36c244bd6ddae80355923cb9738db8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C) \\: 142}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"71\" height=\"29\" /> is the closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by far, and thus, can be relatively certain this is the answer. \n</p><p>~thinker123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=vsE_ezaV4Xs\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=vsE_ezaV4Xs</a>\n~Punxsutawney Phil\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjQARBvdZ20\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjQARBvdZ20</a>\n~Hawk Math\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YxWjDcUcaeQ&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=13\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YxWjDcUcaeQ&amp;list=PLexHyfQ8DMuKqltG3cHT7Di4jhVl6L4YJ&amp;index=13</a>\n~Answer Choice\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HkwgH9Lc1hE\">https://youtu.be/HkwgH9Lc1hE</a>\n</p><p>~OmegaLearn\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/CTXQunZpBA4\">https://youtu.be/CTXQunZpBA4</a>\n</p><p>~TheBeautyofMath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A\">2021 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems